export anchor AirmailStyle:
    number: 119
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Airmail
    idea: The dashboard is an airmail envelope addressed to Mara, with red and blue chevron edges, a par avion label, postcode boxes for the numbers, and each project flying a dashed route towards its due date.
    base: light
    palette:
        sky: #e8eef7, the page behind the envelope
        envelope: #f8fafd, the main surface
        tissueBlue: #eef3fa, aerogramme cards and rows
        ink: #1b2433, text and postcode digits
        muted: #4c5868, captions and the dashed part of a route still to fly
        airmailRed: #b3202a, chevrons, the primary button, overdue, Behind and this week
        airmailBlue: #1f3e8c, chevrons, the par avion label, the brand, the flown route, At risk and focus
        green: #1f6a45, the On track label
        rule: #c5d0e0, dividers and card edges
    type:
        Two stacks. Geometric is Futura, Century Gothic, Avenir Next,
        Avenir, URW Gothic, Trebuchet MS, sans-serif, for labels, names,
        digits and buttons, often caps with 0.1em tracking. Letter is
        Georgia, Iowan Old Style, Times New Roman, serif, for the greeting
        and body. Sizes are 34px Georgia italic greeting, 30px bold
        geometric postcode digits, 26px bold percent, 18px bold project
        names, 12 to 14px geometric caps labels and 15 to 17px body.
    layout:
        The whole dashboard sits inside a 14px border of red, white and blue
        diagonal chevrons. The top left has a blue Par avion, By airmail
        label and the brand in blue and red, with caps nav links under it,
        the current one red with a small paper plane mark and an underline.
        The top right has a dashed Postage paid box with a round blue
        postmark reading 31 OCT 2026 and cancel lines. A ruled tools row
        holds a pill search, a red pill New project button, a round bell and
        the user. The letter opens with Dear Mara in italic, the date line
        and a red urgent line, beside a To address block with a red left
        bar. The four figures are written one digit per red or blue outlined
        postcode box. Six aerogramme cards follow in three columns, each
        with a chevron strip on top, the name, an italic care of team line,
        a route from Start to the due date where a filled plane sits at the
        percent along a dashed line, the percent flown, the task count and a
        status label. The chart is a flight log line, last week dashed blue
        with hollow circles and this week solid red with diamonds, values on
        each point. Correspondence lists activity with envelope icons.
        Cards go two across below 1000px and one across below 700px.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24 to 30px envelope padding, 18px between cards, 32px before sections.
    density: Airy. A letter opening, one row of postcodes, cards with one route each.
    corners: Square envelope and cards. Pill buttons, search and fields at 20px. Round bell and avatar.
    borders: A 14px chevron border round the envelope, an 8px chevron strip on each card top, 2px postcode boxes and a dashed stamp box.
    shadows: One soft blue shadow under the envelope and a 2px flat lip under cards.
    icons:
        A filled plane rides each route. Labels pair the caps word with a
        filled circle for On track, a diamond on a dashed label for At risk
        and a square on a solid red label for Behind. A clock marks overdue
        and envelope outlines mark activity.
    focus: A 3px blue outline offset 3px with a 6px soft red halo.
    tone: Warm letter writing, such as Dear Mara, Projects in transit and Correspondence.
